s as read. my dot and mac do a lot of notications and having to click through all the chats is a bit annoying.", "url": "https://x.com/BlindsidedEve/status/2115916076240539997"}, {"author_id": "2654853294", "created_at": "2026-10-29T21:15:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115915570009030987"], "id": "2115915570009030987", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Our @ChatGPT plugin has been published! Now you can get UV Index forecasts from ChatGPT/dots\n\nhttps://t.co/vBnmHSI68y", "url": "https://x.com/techno246/status/2115915570009030987"}, {"author_id": "2104011501606776832", "created_at": "2026-10-29T21:14:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115915274520342872"], "id": "2115915274520342872", "in_reply_to_user_id": "58865213", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115855769665147254", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ajambrosino when I open a window on my dot I would love if it was still there when I came back to my dot after checking another chat.", "url": "https://x.com/BlindsidedEve/status/2115915274520342872"}, {"author_id": "1818728962706829312", "created_at": "2026-10-29T21:12:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115914784831164664"], "id": "2115914784831164664", "in_reply_to_user_id": "58865213", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115855769665147254", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ajambrosino My Dot often tells me \"My cloud browser is temporarily unavailable\".", "url": "https://x.com/S86067S/status/2115914784831164664"}, {"author_id": "1499122069275127808", "created_at": "2026-10-29T21:12:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115914709677621592"], "id": "2115914709677621592", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 53, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My dot just did my Duolingo", "url": "https://x.com/bitcoinaqua/status/2115914709677621592"}, {"author_id": "23454758", "created_at": "2026-10-29T21:10:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115914274543665571"], "id": "2115914274543665571", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "my Dot is officially nerf'd, 30 minutes since last reply @OpenAI @ChatGPT @thsottiaux @OpenAIDevs", "url": "https://x.com/PeterJ_Medina/status/2115914274543665571"}, {"author_id": "49339648", "created_at": "2026-10-29T21:08:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115913807910609173"], "id": "2115913807910609173", "in_reply_to_user_id": "58865213", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115855769665147254", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ajambrosino CUSTOM DOT GREETINGS.\n\n1. Adults (professionals) within earshot. 2. I call my dot. 3. The dot is pretty-much, like, \u201cwhat\u2019s up bro, what\u2019s goin\u2019 on bro, how\u2019ve you been my guy, so like, whatcha feel like doing, broski?\u201d 4. Fuuccckkkkkkk. \n\nMake customizable (I\u2019ve tried\u2026) \n\nI\u2019d", "url": "https://x.com/RobbieLemos/status/2115913807910609173"}, {"author_id": "2464843704", "created_at": "2026-10-29T21:07:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115913499943838194"], "id": "2115913499943838194", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 273, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "My dot went on an unnanounced break of unspecified duration! @thsottiaux maybe a warning would have been nice. There are a bunch of projects my dot was coordinating that are now all in limbo. Sad. All the major physics breakthroughs I could have made \u2026", "url": "https://x.com/karch_andreas/status/2115913499943838194"}, {"author_id": "533199190", "created_at": "2026-10-29T20:53:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115909827855630513"], "id": "2115909827855630513", "in_reply_to_user_id": "58865213", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115855769665147254", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ajambrosino I want my dot to be able to access multiple computers at once instead of just one at at time.", "url": "https://x.com/HomeFreeHatGuy/status/2115909827855630513"}, {"author_id": "3201565120", "created_at": "2026-10-29T20:51:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115909414993674674"], "id": "2115909414993674674", "in_reply_to_user_id": "3201565120", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115909362308816981", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ajambrosino 8/ Fewer repetitive permission prompts. If I ask my dot to do something, that should authorise the normal steps needed to complete it. Ask again when the scope or risk changes, not for every action within the task I\u2019ve already approved.", "url": "https://x.com/NotGMO_me/status/2115909414993674674"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115909304381239296"]}, "author_id": "14443982", "created_at": "2026-10-29T20:51:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115909358454517907"], "id": "2115909358454517907", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I love my Dot but I can get along with Duet just fine. Nice personality to boot! https://t.co/PhElMqzW6c", "url": "https://x.com/YiJingMan/status/2115909358454517907"}, {"author_id": "19684607927031